{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A wall from this side and a wall from that side.</b> Some interpret it: the wall is the heap (גל) that served as witness between Jacob and Laban the Aramean, and we say: he is Balaam, he is Laban, he is Kushan Rish'atayim. And he now went and crossed over the heap for evil against Israel, to curse them; therefore the heap that had been witness between them came to harm him, as it is written: ״and she pressed Balaam's foot against the wall (הקיר)״ — that is the heap, that is the wall. And because of this he became lame, as is stated: ״וילך שפי״."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase וילך שפי (literally 'and he went lame') appears to be a biblical quotation or allusion, but its source is uncertain; rendered literally without resolving."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:21.481315114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}